{
  "id": "i01-l01",
  "unit": "i01-catching-up",
  "title": "When I was small",
  "status": "draft",
  "tip": "**Used to**: verb stem + **-তাম** for আমি and আমরা.\n\n- থাকা → **থাকতাম** 'I used to live'\n- খেলা → **খেলতাম**, পড়া → **পড়তাম**, করা → **করতাম**\n- যাওয়া changes its stem: **যেতাম** 'I used to go'\n\nUse it for things that happened again and again, or went on for a long time: **ছোটবেলায় আমি গ্রামে থাকতাম** 'When I was small, I lived in the village'. For one finished event, keep the simple past: **গেলাম** 'I went'.\n\nNegative: **না** after the verb: **থাকতাম না** 'I didn't use to live'. Never -নি here.\n\n**বড় হয়েছি** 'I grew up' uses the perfect: **আমি ঢাকায় বড় হয়েছি**.",
  "vocab": [
